🔹 4. Bounded Generics

Restricts allowed types.

---

📌 Example

```java id="g12"
class Calculator<T extends Number> {

    T number;

    Calculator(T number) {
        this.number = number;
    }
}
```

---

# ✔ Allowed

```java id="g13"
Calculator<Integer> c1 =
        new Calculator<>(10);

Calculator<Double> c2 =
        new Calculator<>(5.5);
```

---

❌ Not Allowed

```java id="g14"
Calculator<String> c3 =
        new Calculator<>("Java");
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 5. Wildcards

Represent unknown types.

---

📌 Unbounded Wildcard

```java id="g15"
List<?> list;
```

---

📌 Upper Bounded Wildcard

```java id="g16"
List<? extends Number> list;
```

---

📌 Lower Bounded Wildcard

```java id="g17"
List<? super Integer> list;
```

